Subject: Initialize regex state before its first move

Local correction for libc++ 10.0.1; not an upstream backport.
The default state is moved into a container before __at_first_ is assigned.
Initialize the bool rather than suppressing the GCC 13.2 uninitialized warning.
Validated with regex state, matching, searching and replacement tests.

--- a/regex
+++ b/regex
@@ -1342,7 +1342,7 @@
     _LIBCPP_INLINE_VISIBILITY
     __state()
         : __do_(0), __first_(nullptr), __current_(nullptr), __last_(nullptr),
-          __node_(nullptr), __flags_() {}
+          __node_(nullptr), __flags_(), __at_first_(false) {}
 };
 
 // __node
